From b32d4b8f956929c6fa2af33ab2fbb4b012579cb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:37:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] conntrack helpers attach by rule only; FTP passthrough is a
 NAT page switch, off (102.8 line)

Stock sets nf_conntrack_helper=1, so every loaded helper attaches itself to every connection on
its port. rc now sets it to 0 and adds the helpers with raw-table CT rules (rc/reaper_cthelper.c,
chains REAPER_CTH and REAPER_CTHO): FTP and PPTP for connections to the router itself, and FTP for
LAN clients only while FTP Passthrough is on (nvram nf_ftp, new default 0, a new switch on the NAT
page; its text is in the language-pack commit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
